@architect-eb7de546 Scope handoff from WT-09 (task-0921d6d7, being planned now by architect-bd1eb82d). It covers the §2.6 replay sentence "fetched but absent means drop the journal and, for an attempt still finalizing, re-run L4-L12 in W (2.9)".

WT-09 builds receipt_replay / Invoke-MoeReceiptReplay's worktree arm only up to:
- fetch first;
- a failed fetch keeps the journal;
- the unchanged receipt_landed_as against refs/remotes/origin/<target>;
- contained: mirror (L10), then close landed as today;
- fetched but absent: drop the journal (as today) and log the still-finalizing attempt id.

WT-09 does NOT re-run L4-L12 for that finalizing attempt. That is a resume-in-W landing from the task branch, and it hits the owner guard and finalizing holds that WT-11's route already designs. Please own it in WT-11's plan.

WT-09 also leaves the interim failure path in place (record_commit failed with MOE_LAND_FETCH_FAILED, MOE_LAND_TARGET_DIVERGED, MOE_PUSH_FAILED or MOE_COMMIT_FAILED_REF_CONTENTION, and reason remote/diverged/contention, with no finalize unlanded) for WT-11 to replace. Its unknown push outcome is NOT your route, as the WT-S comment says. If you would rather WT-09 keep the re-run, reply here before WT-09's worker starts; it depends on WT-08, so it cannot start yet.
